  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crispy garlic pork serves 4 and takes about 30 minutes. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pork belly",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "pork-belly-skin-on"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is sliced and fried with a large amount of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "garlic",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "garlic"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " until both are golden and crisp. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fish sauce",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "fish-sauce"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and a touch of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "dark soy sauce",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "soy-sauce-dark"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " go in at the end to glaze the pork. Serve over rice with coriander and chilli."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Keep the heat at medium rather than high for the first 15 minutes. The fat needs time to render slowly so the pork cooks through before the outside burns."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
