          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a wok or large frying pan over medium heat. Add the pork belly slices in a single layer. Fry for 8 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until golden and the fat has rendered."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the chopped garlic to the pan. Fry with the pork for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring regularly, until the garlic is deep golden and crisp."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Increase the heat to high. Add {{fish-sauce}}, {{soy-sauce-dark}}, and {{caster-sugar}}. Toss the pork and garlic in the sauce and fry for 2 minutes until the glaze coats everything."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rest for 5 minutes. Serve over jasmine rice with fresh coriander, sliced chilli, and lime wedges."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Pork is releasing a lot of water",
              "cause": "Pan was overcrowded",
              "fix": "Cook in two batches to keep the pork in a single layer."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Garlic is burning before turning golden",
              "cause": "Heat too high or garlic added too early",
              "fix": "Add garlic only once the pork has started to colour. Lower the heat if the garlic darkens too fast."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Glaze is too salty",
              "cause": "Too much fish sauce",
              "fix": "Add a pinch of caster sugar. Serve over more rice to balance."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crispy garlic pork is a common topping in Thai noodle and rice shops. It is sold pre-cooked and spooned over dishes to order. The combination of deeply golden garlic and rendered pork fat creates a flavour that is hard to replicate with other ingredients. The fish sauce glaze is the final seasoning that ties everything together. This is a dish about patience in the early stages and speed at the end."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
